<title>USA: IBM reports stronger-than-expected earnings.</title>
<headline>IBM reports stronger-than-expected earnings.</headline>
<dateline>ARMONK, N.Y. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp. Tuesday reported better-than-expected earnings of $3.93 a share the fourth quarter, compared with $3.09 a share for the 1995 quarter.</p>
<p>The world's largest computer maker said net income was $2.0 billion vs. $1.7 billion in the year-ago period. Wall Street analysts had expected earnings of $3.88 a share, on average, according to First Call, which tracks earnings estimates.</p>
